  "interpretation": "In the TB-A05 stylized rooftop-courier transfer context, the readable natural-language production brief and the semantically matched JSON-style structured prompt both received maximum blind-review scores on semantic compliance, aesthetic quality, technical-defect cleanliness, and the primary scene_constraint_fidelity dimension. The variant-minus-control delta was 0.00 on every registered dimension and on the overall mean. No visible prompt-format effect was detected in this run. However, all eight outputs saturated the 5-point review scale, leaving no discriminatory range between conditions. The result is therefore classified as inconclusive rather than as evidence that the two prompt representations are equivalent or that either representation is superior.",
